Track User Consent
The consent that you provide is used for the following two primary purposes:

User identification
Tracking user data
The package has two different ways to determine user consent that enable the collection, documentation and management of your user's privacy choices in order to ensure legal compliance.

Zeotap stores the consent information in the customer profile against their unique Customer ID. For more information on how Zeotap stores and processes consent, you can refer to the Consent Management feature of Zeotap.

Default Opt-in
In this scenario, you directly provide consent to Zeotap by setting the opt_out flag to true or false.

For all these three purposes, if the opt_out flag is set to true, then it indicates that you have not granted access to Zeotap. Here, package is not allowed to perform user identification or tracking user data. However, if the opt_out flag is set to false, then the package is allowed to perform all the above actions.

